  "fix_commit": "ec92178a691a10b4b0076556d05daf69ec158200",
  "issue": {
    "author": "JoelR_VC",
    "body_normalized": "### System Information\n\nOperating system: Windows-11-10.0.26200-SP0 64 Bits\nGraphics card: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 NVIDIA Corporation NVIDIA 596.36 Vulkan Backend\n\n### Blender Version\n\nBroken version: 5.2.0 LTS Beta, branch: blender-v5.2-release, commit date: 2026-06-12 12:31, hash: `30341a1f775f`\nWorked: 5.1\n\n### Description of the Issue\n\nIf I activate the transmission in the principled bsdf for a material, the reflections suddenly don't follow the value set for roughness and look like zero roughness. Also, a spot appears on the object at high roughness values. It seems to be the shadow of the object that somehow change to that shape when I turn of the transmission, that can be proved if I look at the render pass of shadows.\n\n<video src=\"attachments/09086c43-e792-4e05-9d9b-4e0f0e5f7033\" title=\"2026-06-13 19-18-30.mp4\" controls></video>\n\n### Steps to Reproduce the Issue\n\n- Open the blend file [transmission_broke.blend](/attachments/46488fcd-8c5f-4a6b-b544-109fc2683e55)\n- in render mode change the roughness value to see if the shader reacts correctly.\n- turn on and off the transmission slider completely to see when the roughness changes, also to see the spot on the object appear.\n- Look at the render mode render passes, the shadow pass, to see that the dark spot is a shadow.",
    "body_raw": "### System Information\n\nOperating system: Windows-11-10.0.26200-SP0 64 Bits\nGraphics card: NVIDIA GeForce RTX 3060 NVIDIA Corporation NVIDIA 596.36 Vulkan Backend\n\n### Blender Version\n\nBroken version: 5.2.0 LTS Beta, branch: blender-v5.2-release, commit date: 2026-06-12 12:31, hash: `30341a1f775f`\nWorked: 5.1\n\n### Description of the Issue\n\nIf I activate the transmission in the principled bsdf for a material, the reflections suddenly don't follow the value set for roughness and look like zero roughness. Also, a spot appears on the object at high roughness values. It seems to be the shadow of the object that somehow change to that shape when I turn of the transmission, that can be proved if I look at the render pass of shadows.\n\n<video src=\"attachments/09086c43-e792-4e05-9d9b-4e0f0e5f7033\" title=\"2026-06-13 19-18-30.mp4\" controls></video>\n\n### Steps to Reproduce the Issue\n\n- Open the blend file [transmission_broke.blend](/attachments/46488fcd-8c5f-4a6b-b544-109fc2683e55)\n- in render mode change the roughness value to see if the shader reacts correctly.\n- turn on and off the transmission slider completely to see when the roughness changes, also to see the spot on the object appear.\n- Look at the render mode render passes, the shadow pass, to see that the dark spot is a shadow.\n\n",
    "body_sha256": "909584814644176e4bcbc6873484b1fb5efc72339112f83d2896972952fc9640",
